  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I understand we have to have the feature of Panic Mode. However, I am pretty sure there are a lot of people who accidentally activate panic mode. I have seen a lot of new user accidentally activated the panic mode and don't know how to get everything back. I tried to tell him how to get it back, but you know, he muted me by panic mode, so there's no way to tell him.\n\nWhen you accidentally turn panic mode on, what you have to do is :\n\n(1) turn on the menu\n(2) click safety button\n(3) change custom setting as it used to be for a user trust rank\n(4) repeat (3) 5 times more, there're six kinds of trust rank\n\nlife is short and you don't want to waste your time. \n\nWhat I suggest is simple:\n\n1. Separate Panic Mode from Shield level custom. (Use Maximum level or just separate this from trust system)\n\n2. Restore Button which makes you get everything back without open a menu, or by just one click on menu. \n\n3. Show user clearly and consistently that he is in panic mode right now.",
